From ff8cdd643b0a031efe9b584dc1307df69974dbd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:08:53 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] gui: the RTK tab says what Codex's sandbox setting is, and
 reads its count when it comes back into view (#3320, Glanci-0525)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sandbox line on Library → RTK turned Codex's config field into a
verdict: [windows] sandbox = "unelevated" made the card say the sandbox
"can't write RTK's history: what RTK saves there isn't recorded", even
while the count beside it had the savings RTK did read. A config file says
where Codex is set to run its commands, not whether a write failed — and a
session may run unrestricted whatever the config says. The line now says
what is actually known: "Codex is set to run its commands in its Windows
sandbox…", in both wordings (elevated and unelevated), through t() in all
five languages (en, zh, zh-TW, ja, de) with no placeholders.

The count is also stale while the page stays put: loadRTK ran only when the
tab was opened, so a command run since wasn't shown until the reader
switched tabs and back. The RTK panel is now re-read at the same moments
the rest of the page already re-reads (quietLoad's visibilitychange and
focus, and the page's open hook) — no new timer. A re-read is held off
while a switch, install, upgrade or PATH change is under way, so it cannot
cover the answer of one of those with older state, and loadRTK's own
rtkLoading keeps requests from overlapping.

The Windows half is not verified here: no real Windows box with Codex's
sandbox ran under this fix, so the change is the wording (a setting said as
a setting) and the refresh, as the issue's own evidence (rtk gain readable
while the warning stayed) called for.

Red, without the fix: node --test internal/gui/tests/library-rtk-gain.test.cjs
-> all 8 assertions fail: the sandbox line reads "Codex runs its commands in
its Windows sandbox, which can't write…" (a verdict), and the count isn't
reread on the window coming back (verified in a clean export of the base
with the new test: 0/8 pass; with the fix: 8/8 on Chromium and WebKit).

Green: same command, 8/8; the six other library-rtk suites 104/104; go test
-tags nogui ./internal/gui/ -run 'CoreScriptBudget|I18n|Strings|Plugin' ok
(app.js untouched, the core budget unchanged); go build -tags nogui ./... ok.
